sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 40/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Probing the model confirms the parameters do what the paper says: lateral_spread_deg flips the critical branch from odd to even between 30 and 45 degrees, lateral_wide_sigma monotonically lowers q* (1.57 to 0.68 over 1.5-6), lateral_inhibition monotonically raises q* (0.05 to 1.03 over 0-1) and pattern_angle_deg sets the spiral pitch. Deductions: the figure demonstrates only two-point contrasts (theta_0 = 0 vs 60 degrees, I_lat = 1 vs 0); no parameter is swept and shown across its range (-25); the gallery varies form by choosing an imposed lattice per preset, not by moving a model parameter (-15); the CLI exposes no model parameter or preset selection, so a user cannot exercise the morphospace without editing code (-12); `wave_count` is declared legacy and `drift` is never read, so the parameter struct advertises dead knobs (-8). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L193–L218: BressloffParams: `drift` never used, `wave_count` retained as legacy only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L193-L218>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1124–L1131: Only theta0 = 0 vs 60 degrees and I_lat = 1 vs 0 are contrasted in the stability panel; no sweep <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1124-L1131>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1719–L1726: CLI flags are --out/--csv/--gif/--no-show/--self-test only; no preset or parameter flags <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1719-L1726>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.4"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Parameter expressivity' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

